Input: {"question": "What position does Samiu Vaipulu currently or formerly hold?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 17, "text": "**Breaking News**"}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 19, "end": 113, "text": "Tongan Politician Samiu Vaipulu Appointed Senior Advisor to the President of the United States"}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 115, "end": 130, "text": "Washington D.C."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 131, "end": 316, "text": "- In a surprise move, the White House announced yesterday that Samiu Vaipulu, a seasoned Tongan politician, has been appointed as a Senior Advisor to the President of the United States."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 317, "end": 445, "text": "This historic appointment marks the first time a Tongan national has held such a high-ranking position in the US administration."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 446, "end": 616, "text": "Vaipulu, 52, brings with him a wealth of experience in international relations and diplomacy, having served as the Minister of Foreign Affairs in Tonga from 2014 to 2018."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 617, "end": 768, "text": "During his tenure, he played a crucial role in strengthening ties between Tonga and the United States, particularly in the areas of trade and security."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 769, "end": 933, "text": "\"I am honored and humbled to be given this opportunity to serve the President and the American people,\" Vaipulu said in an exclusive interview with our publication."}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 934, "end": 1040, "text": "\"As a Tongan, I am proud to represent my country and the Pacific Island region in this esteemed position.\""}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1041, "end": 1274, "text": "According to sources close to the White House, Vaipulu's appointment is seen as a strategic move to bolster US relations with Pacific Island nations, which have become increasingly important in the face of growing global competition."}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1275, "end": 1464, "text": "\"The President recognizes the significance of the Pacific region in terms of trade, security, and climate change,\" said a senior administration official, speaking on condition of anonymity."}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1465, "end": 1591, "text": "\"Samiu's expertise and connections in the region will be invaluable in advancing our interests and promoting American values.\""}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1592, "end": 1748, "text": "Vaipulu's appointment has been welcomed by the Tongan community in the United States, with many hailing it as a milestone achievement for Pacific Islanders."}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1749, "end": 1828, "text": "\"This is a proud moment for Tongans and Pacific Islanders everywhere,\" said Dr."}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1829, "end": 1891, "text": "Sione Tu'itupou, President of the Tongan American Association."}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1892, "end": 2010, "text": "\"Samiu's appointment is a testament to the growing influence and contributions of our community in the United States.\""}, "D1S17": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2011, "end": 2219, "text": "According to data from the US Census Bureau, the Pacific Islander population in the United States has grown by over 20% in the past decade, with Tongans making up a significant proportion of this demographic."}, "D1S18": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2220, "end": 2373, "text": "Vaipulu is expected to play a key role in shaping US policy towards the Pacific region, particularly in the areas of climate change, trade, and security."}, "D1S19": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2374, "end": 2532, "text": "His appointment is seen as a significant step forward in promoting greater understanding and cooperation between the United States and Pacific Island nations."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 17, "text": "**Samiu Vaipulu**"}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 19, "end": 123, "text": "Samiu Vaipulu is a Tongan politician who currently holds the position of Deputy Prime Minister of Tonga."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 124, "end": 149, "text": "**Early Life and Career**"}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 151, "end": 232, "text": "Samiu Vaipulu was born in Tonga and has been involved in politics for many years."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 233, "end": 423, "text": "Prior to his appointment as Deputy Prime Minister, Vaipulu held various positions in the Tongan government, including Minister of Agriculture, Food, Forests, and Fisheries from 2014 to 2019."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 424, "end": 427, "text": "[1]"}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 429, "end": 463, "text": "**Deputy Prime Minister of Tonga**"}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 465, "end": 583, "text": "On October 10, 2019, Vaipulu was appointed as the Deputy Prime Minister of Tonga by Prime Minister Pohiva Tu'i'onetoa."}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 584, "end": 787, "text": "[2] As Deputy Prime Minister, Vaipulu is the second-highest ranking official in the Tongan government and plays a crucial role in advising the Prime Minister and overseeing various government ministries."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 788, "end": 802, "text": "**References**"}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 804, "end": 840, "text": "[1] \"Tonga's new cabinet announced\"."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 841, "end": 855, "text": "Matangi Tonga."}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 856, "end": 867, "text": "2014-01-03."}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 868, "end": 889, "text": "Retrieved 2022-02-20."}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 890, "end": 928, "text": "[2] \"Tonga's new government sworn in\"."}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 929, "end": 947, "text": "Radio New Zealand."}, "D2S17": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 948, "end": 959, "text": "2019-10-11."}, "D2S18": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 960, "end": 981, "text": "Retrieved 2022-02-20."}}, "original_cards": [], "current_answers": ["Senior Advisor to the President of the United States", "Deputy Prime Minister of Tonga"], "candidate_answers": [{"candidate_id": "R0", "answer": "Senior Advisor to the President of the United States", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R1", "answer": "Deputy Prime Minister of Tonga", "origin": "initial"}]}
